    {
      "executionState" : "enabled",
      "id" : "note",
      "kind" : "edit.markdownNote",
      "parameters" : {
        "text" : "# Crater Duel · Generated textures\nA turn-based artillery duel across a destructible ridge. On each Run, one fixed-seed FLUX.2 Klein 4B Distilled job generates the soil at 1024 × 1024, and four fixed-seed SDXS 512 jobs generate the meadow turf, the bedrock, the tank armor plate, and the dusk sky backdrop. Asset Cache stores the five images as named slots for this run and previews each one as it becomes ready. The duel starts after all five are ready; later frames reuse the bundle without invoking either model again. Cancel and Run starts a fresh cache and regenerates all five. Both model packages remain link-only.\n\n**Controls.** Drag the Trackpad crosshair, or drag on the full-screen preview, to aim your green tank on the left: the direction from its turret to the crosshair sets the barrel angle, and the distance sets the power (both are shown top left). The dotted guide shows the start of the arc without wind. Press Action or Space to fire.\n\n**Goal.** Shells fall under gravity and drift with the wind shown at the top. Every blast carves a crater and damages nearby tanks; tanks drop into craters dug beneath them. The red enemy fires back and tightens its aim after each shot, so strike first. Destroy it to win the round, then press Space for a new ridge; win five rounds to conquer the ridge. Score counts damage dealt, direct hits, and round bonuses for remaining armor and few shots. If your tank is destroyed, press Space to start a new campaign.\n\n**Settings.** The game settings JSON sets `windStrength` (0 calm, 1 normal, up to 3), `enemySkill` (1 normal; higher aims better), and `roundsToWin` (1–9). Changing a setting restarts the duel."
      },
      "resources" : {},
      "title" : "How to play"
    },
